  "articleBody": "Building an addition is an exciting investment, but framing errors at the junction where new meets old can create persistent structural and moisture problems.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid:\n- Starting without approved building permits: Beginning excavation or wall assembly prior to permit issuance risks work stop-orders and steep compliance fines.\n- Treating the addition as structurally independent: Failing to properly anchor new wall studs, floor joists, and roof rafters into the existing structure causes separation over time.\n- Creating mismatched floor heights: Miscalculating sill plates or joist depths creates awkward step-downs or tripping hazards between living spaces.\n- Skipping weatherproofing at the tie-in: Omitting proper flashing and water-resistive barriers where new framing joins existing exterior walls leads to hidden water damage.\n- Enclosing walls before framing sign-off: Adding insulation and drywall before framing and rough-in inspections are approved violates code and triggers delays.\n\nHow to Compare Your Options:\nChoose a contractor who understands structural tie-ins and directly leads the framing and finish phases. \n\nLooking to expand your home without the stress? Reach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to get started on your addition.",
